From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:32:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2516/3799] soh: rename func_800F7208 ->
 Audio_ResetSequencesAndSfx

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: resets the active sequences and channel state and restarts the SFX player
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_general.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_general.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_general.c b/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
index 4ffe33a2d..404544a54 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_general.c
@@ -5605,7 +5605,8 @@ void Audio_ResetForSpecChange(s32 arg0) {
     Audio_ResetSounds();
 }
 
-void func_800F7208(void) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_800F7208: resets the active sequences and channel state and restarts the SFX player
+void Audio_ResetSequencesAndSfx(void) {
     Audio_ResetActiveSequences();
     Audio_QueueCmdS32(0xF2000000, 1);
     Audio_ResetData();
-- 
